stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Waiting: Job Added to Queue
    
    Waiting --> Active: Worker Picks Up Job
    Waiting --> Delayed: Scheduled for Future
    Waiting --> Prioritized: High Priority Job
    
    Delayed --> Waiting: Delay Elapsed
    Prioritized --> Active: Worker Available
    
    Active --> Processing: Job Handler Executing
    
    Processing --> Completed: Success
    Processing --> Failed: Error Thrown
    Processing --> Stalled: Worker Timeout/Crash
    
    Failed --> Waiting: Retry (Attempts < Max)
    Failed --> DeadLetter: Max Retries Reached
    Failed --> Failed: Exponential Backoff
    
    Stalled --> Waiting: Job Recovered
    Stalled --> Failed: Recovery Failed
    
    Completed --> [*]: Job Finished Successfully
    DeadLetter --> ManualReview: Requires Intervention
    ManualReview --> Waiting: Manually Retried
    ManualReview --> Archived: Permanently Failed
    
    Archived --> [*]
    
    note right of Waiting
        State: WAITING
        - Job is in queue
        - Ready to be processed
        - Can be prioritized
        - Default TTL: indefinite
    end note
    
    note right of Active
        State: ACTIVE
        - Locked by a worker
        - Processing in progress
        - Has timeout protection
        - Prevents double processing
    end note
    
    note right of Processing
        State: PROCESSING
        - Handler function executing
        - Can report progress
        - Can update job data
        - Monitored by worker
    end note
    
    note right of Completed
        State: COMPLETED
        - Successfully processed
        - Result stored (optional)
        - Auto-removed based on config
        - Metrics recorded
    end note
    
    note right of Failed
        State: FAILED
        - Processing failed
        - Error logged
        - Retry with backoff
        - Attempts tracked
    end note
    
    note right of Delayed
        State: DELAYED
        - Scheduled for future
        - Timestamp-based activation
        - Use cases: Reminders,
          Scheduled tasks,
          Rate limiting
    end note
    
    note right of DeadLetter
        State: DEAD LETTER
        - All retries exhausted
        - Manual intervention needed
        - Logged for analysis
        - Can be replayed
    end note
    
    note right of Stalled
        State: STALLED
        - Worker crashed/timeout
        - Job recovery process
        - Automatic retry possible
        - Prevents job loss
    end note
